    <key>NSLocationUsageDescription</key>
    <string>macOS classifies Wi-Fi network names as location data. Access is used only to read the SSID and BSSID of the network this Mac is already connected to. No location is recorded, stored or transmitted.</string>
    <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
    <string>macOS classifies Wi-Fi network names as location data. Access is used only to read the SSID and BSSID of the network this Mac is already connected to. No location is recorded, stored or transmitted.</string>
    <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
    <string>WifiHigh5 uses network access only for features you start yourself: router reachability, LAN discovery, and an optional Internet speed test. LAN discovery shows its target and asks for confirmation. The speed test sends only generated test bytes to Cloudflare; no files, Wi-Fi names, labels, or notes are uploaded.</string>
